[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468832156","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468832156","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468832156,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TJ2Oc","user":{"login":"ettiSurreal","id":98223724,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdrGbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98223724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal","html_url":"https://github.com/ettiSurreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T18:53:49Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T18:53:49Z","body":"Negative delta is intended to move towards the opposite angle (as stated by the docs), so this is indented behavior, it wasn't originally in the old PR though. I think it was assumed that the oscillation that occurred at the midway point would've been considered a bug so I \"fixed\" it after being given a different implementation by @kleonc, originally I even suggested adding 180 degrees to the target as a workaround for that in the old PR. So if the oscillation should to be the correct behavior that can be changed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468832156/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468843069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468843069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468843069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TJ449","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T19:00:59Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T19:18:10Z","body":"Going in the opposite direction and reaching the wrong target are two different things. The opposite direction might mean a path that is not the shortest, but at least should not reach the wrong target in term of rotation.\r\n\r\n> I think it was assumed that the oscillation that occurred at the midway point would've been considered a bug so I \"fixed\" it after being given a different implementation by @kleonc\r\n\r\nDoes the oscillation mean when the shortest path switches due to target movement? If so, such a problem should not occur if positive delta is interpreted as a counterclockwise rotation statically instead of an angle toward the shortest path, although compatibility will be broken. You can consider making it an optional argument `rotate_toward(float p_from, float p_to, float p_delta, bool p_shortest = true)` or a separate API like `rotate_toward_counterclockwise()` to prevent compatibility breakdown.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468843069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468980263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468980263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468980263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKaYn","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:36:18Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T20:38:47Z","body":"This is the code snippet of `rotate_toward()`\r\n\r\n``` c++\r\nstatic _ALWAYS_INLINE_ double rotate_toward(double p_from, double p_to, double p_delta) {\r\n\tdouble difference = Math::angle_difference(p_from, p_to);\r\n\tdouble abs_difference = Math::abs(difference);\r\n\t// When `p_delta < 0` move no further than to PI radians away from `p_to` (as PI is the max possible angle distance).\r\n\treturn p_from + CLAMP(p_delta, abs_difference - Math_PI, abs_difference) * (difference >= 0.0 ? 1.0 : -1.0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I guess it _is_ intentional.\r\nMy take is that `move_towards()` with negative delta moves the value as far from `p_to` as possible, so the author wanted the angle to go as far from `p_to` as possible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468980263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468981969","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468981969","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468981969,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKazR","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:37:37Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T20:38:55Z","body":"@PhairZ I'm pointing out that the intent was wrong from the beginning. The direction of rotation is correct, but the destination angle is wrong.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468981969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468985596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468985596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468985596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKbr8","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:40:21Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T20:41:03Z","body":"@TokageItLab I think i disagree. -delta is intended to go as far as possible from target, not in the opposite direction.\r\nworking around it is also not that much of a hassle since you can just multiply target by the sign of delta.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468985596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468990393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468990393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468990393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKc25","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:43:56Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T21:28:01Z","body":"@PhairZ In that case, simply pass the inverted target as an argument, instead of inverting delta, as mentioned above. This can be accomplished in a few lines of code, so it does not have much worth of utility function.\r\n\r\nConversely, arbitrarily rotating the longest path cannot be accomplished in a few lines of code, so the behavior makes sense as a utility function.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468990393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468997644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2468997644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2468997644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKeoM","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:49:17Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T20:49:17Z","body":"Alright, I'll open a PR on this issue. It's up to the contributers to merge it or not. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468997644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469021195","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2469021195","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2469021195,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKkYL","user":{"login":"ettiSurreal","id":98223724,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdrGbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98223724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal","html_url":"https://github.com/ettiSurreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T21:06:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T21:08:04Z","body":"> You can consider making it an optional argument `rotate_toward(float p_from, float p_to, float p_delta, bool p_shortest = true)` or a separate API like `rotate_toward_counterclockwise()` to prevent compatibility breakdown.\r\n\r\nNegative delta usage seems like something that'd be very rarely used regardless, plus since getting the old behavior is rather easy this shouldn't be necessary. Otherwise if there are complaints that could just be addressed in a follow-up.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469021195/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469027190","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99083#issuecomment-2469027190","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99083","id":2469027190,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKl12","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T21:11:21Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T21:18:53Z","body":"@ettiSurreal What I mean by compatibility breakdown is that we are talking about oscillation issues, not inverted targets.\r\n\r\nThe behavior of a negative delta reaching an inverted target definitely should be removed, and since there is a migration way of just inverting the target instead of the delta, there is no need to add an option for that.\r\n\r\nThere are two ways to go about what to treat as \"positive\" delta (shortest rotation is positobe, or mathematical positive radian is positive), and I think both are valid.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469027190/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]